1
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,480
Thank you.

2
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:03,680
Thank you.

3
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:33,740
X-V-Mon and I decided to
take on Malomyotismon,

4
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,857
even though the others were afraid of him.

5
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:36,917
I don't blame them.

6
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,647
If I ever stopped to think about
anything, I'd be scared, too.

7
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:43,017
Malomyotismon played
mind tricks on everyone,

8
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:46,257
terrifying Ken and making the others
believe their favorite wish had come true.

9
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:48,077
But my wish really did come true,

10
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:51,748
because V-Mon digivolved into
all his forms at the same time.

11
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:53,095
That's the good news.

12
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:56,557
The bad news is that Malomyotismon's
wishes are also coming true,

13
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:00,111
And his wishes could make a
genie crawl back in his bottle!

14
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,740
Otrago, there's got a lot of gold!

15
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:14,597
It's so dark, and it'll be like this
forever if we can't stop Malamiotismon.

16
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,240
No, I can't give up hope.

17
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,117
I have too many people depending on me.

18
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,540
The two worlds will unite in darkness!

19
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:24,900
Then they shall both be mine!

20
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,226
That's never going to happen.

21
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:28,640
And why not?

22
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:31,717
Because we're going to
stop you once and for all!

23
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,640
You fools!

24
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,607
You think you can defeat me?

25
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:37,377
Your pitiful light is no
match for my darkness.

26
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:39,342
Even now, it consumes the world.

27
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,420
Not for long. Get him!

28
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,860
Positron laser!

29
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,278
Screaming darkness!

30
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,340
They're losing.

31
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,117
And it's all our fault.

32
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,340
Thanks to us,

33
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:58,417
the digital world and the real world
are going to be covered in darkness.

34
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,460
You foolish Digi-Destin.

35
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:02,120
Watch closely now.

36
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:05,880
Your world is being
consumed by Eternal Night.

37
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:07,800
You'll never win.

38
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,335
Even if you defeat us, others
will rise up against you.

39
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,540
Who could possibly beat him?

40
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:15,620
I just want to go home.

41
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:16,840
Why bother?

42
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:18,240
There's no point.

43
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:21,892
I don't think any of us have
a home to go home to anymore.

44
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:25,780
Yeah, there's no point
to anything anymore.

45
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,947
Hey, quit talking like that.

46
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,020
Why, it's all true, isn't it?

47
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,680
There's nothing any of us can do to win.

48
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,040
He's right.

49
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:35,928
There's no point in trying.

50
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:38,182
The only thing we'll do is fail.

51
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:39,360
He beat us.

52
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,774
It's just that simple.

53
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,720
No, he hasn't. Huh?

54
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:45,240
But he will beat us if you give up.

55
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,797
Just because things look bad,
there's no reason not to try.

56
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:49,710
I don't know.

57
00:03:49,793 --> 00:03:54,617
Well, I do, so quit sitting there like a
bunch of zapsacks and let's beat this guy.

58
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:55,920
But what can we do?

59
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,860
He's already defeated us once.

60
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,537
You're right, it's hopeless.

61
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:02,380
In mere moments, both worlds will be mine.

62
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,160
The darkness is strong here, too.

63
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:14,140
I know, but if we want to get back to
the digital world, this is our only way.

64
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:18,854
It might be the only chance for all
of us in both worlds, for everything.

65
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:22,437
But we don't have any idea if
this gate is going to open.

66
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:26,677
With the gate in Tokyo sealed by Black
War and Greymon, this is the closest one.

67
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,737
I know he was trying to help
us protect the digital world.

68
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:33,877
I think he may have done more harm
than good if we can't get back there.

69
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:37,497
It looks like we have no choice but to
give it a try and hope for the best.

70
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:40,277
This is the place where we
first went to the digital world.

71
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,831
Maybe that's a good sign.

72
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,548
Well, this had better work.

73
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,677
We have to get Noriko to
Oikawa as soon as possible.

74
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:50,289
Tell me, what's going to happen
to my daughter if you don't?

75
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:54,740
Don't worry, she'll be fine
But She'll be okay, I promise

76
00:04:55,580 --> 00:05:01,000
Alright, we trust you Am I the only one
who's worried we won't be able to save her?

77
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,632
That we won't be able to save everything?

78
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:06,337
The dying of the light and no one to rage

79
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:09,297
against it My power
over both of the worlds

80
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,797
is growing stronger
And now there's nothing

81
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:14,397
that can stand against
me I don't think so,

82
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,362
positron laser!

83
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:21,100
Start force! Justice speed!

84
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,658
Screaming darkness!

85
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:36,454
Why do they bother trying to fight him?

86
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,537
There's just nothing that they
can do that will defeat him.

87
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:42,057
They should know it's
all pointless by now.

88
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:44,717
Maybe we could help if
we were the Digidestined.

89
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:47,320
But we were only chosen by Oikawa.

90
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,480
It's hopeless.

91
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,337
Tai, we have to get to the digital
world before it's too late.

92
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,250
I know.

93
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:54,434
Hey, I've got an idea.

94
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,500
Digiport, open!

95
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:58,290
Please?

96
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,284
I guess our parents were wrong.

97
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:02,117
That's not the magic word after all.

98
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,280
This is bad, guys.

99
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:04,697
What are we gonna do?

100
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,297
This could be the end of everything.

101
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:07,556
Whoa, wait a minute.

102
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,920
Look at this. Huh?

103
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:10,520
More bad news?

104
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,837
Gates are opening all over the world.

105
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,120
Look, you guys.

106
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:17,654
It's lighting up like a modem
rodder in full pulse mode.

107
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:22,137
Well, if that looks like a Christmas tree
lighting up, I'd have to agree with you.

108
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,050
Look,

109
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:27,626
the light from the gates is cutting through
Malomyotismon's blanket of darkness.

110
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:32,400
It must be coming from Digivices
all over the planet. Just think,

111
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,897
millions of kids are banding together to

112
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:37,920
take a stand against
Malomyotismon right now.

113
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:41,657
It doesn't matter where they're
from or what language they speak.

114
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:44,737
They all knew they had to
unite against the darkness.

115
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:48,057
Had to fight it no matter how
futile it may have seemed.

116
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:51,157
I knew that Malomyotus Mon
couldn't win that easily.

117
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,120
The whole world's fighting him.

118
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:57,450
Look!

119
00:06:57,533 --> 00:06:58,580
So many Digimon!

120
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,637
I hope we don't have to feed them all.

121
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:02,073
There must be hundreds.

122
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,477
The light from the Digivice has guided us.

123
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,457
It led us all here.

124
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:08,370
It's great!

125
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:12,337
The partner Digimon and the DigiDest and
from all over the world are gathering!

126
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,832
We can't allow you to destroy our worlds!

127
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,757
Yeah, you think you can bully us?

128
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:18,077
Well, put up your dukes!

129
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:18,990
Ha!

130
00:07:19,073 --> 00:07:22,720
Your meaningless little gathering
of buffoons doesn't frighten me!

131
00:07:23,260 --> 00:07:27,320
It doesn't matter how many of you
there are, you'll never defeat me!

132
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:28,577
Screaming Darkness!

133
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,490
Yes!

134
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:39,877
We have to fight it, baby,
but I need your help.

135
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,784
I'm right here for you, Palmon!

136
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:46,320
Deramon! Sartaromon! Frigimon! Breezomon!

137
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:47,730
Shakkoumon!

138
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,560
Go! Apemon!

139
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:50,970
Meramon!

140
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:52,290
Crabmon!

141
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:53,830
Lohamon!

142
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:56,220
Yonamon! Whamon! Gokimon!

143
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,510
Gossamons!

144
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:06,680
Wait a minute. What's happening?

145
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,600
The light!

146
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:13,120
It's blinding!

147
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:15,640
No, it can't be!

148
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,080
Hey, look!

149
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,260
He's in pain!

150
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:20,538
The light of the Digimon is winning!

151
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:26,780
Look! In the sky!

152
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,017
That light!

153
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:31,220
Just like three years ago
the cane is opening up.

154
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:32,377
It actually opened.

155
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:33,989
I mean of course it opened

156
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,460
Come on Noriko

157
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:38,920
It's all right

158
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,920
Let's go come on

159
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:55,640
Huh Noriko Noriko, where did she go?

160
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:58,050
Don't you worry.

161
00:08:58,133 --> 00:09:00,317
Your daughter's in the
very best of hands now.

162
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,230
Yes, but...

163
00:09:01,313 --> 00:09:02,657
There's nothing we can really do right now

164
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,877
but believe in the
strength of our children.

165
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:05,790
She's right.

166
00:09:05,873 --> 00:09:06,917
We'll have to trust them.

167
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,777
I'm sure everything will be fine.

168
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:10,837
It all worked out three
years ago, after all.

169
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:11,920
I hope so.

170
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,857
But tell me, what's going to
happen if they don't come back?

171
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:16,277
We can't think like that.

172
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,697
If we want them to succeed,
we have to believe in them.

173
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:20,074
Everyone must believe.

174
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:23,960
Our children and the whole
world might depend on it.

175
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:44,617
All the Digimon have fallen
into some kind of trance.

176
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,657
You look like Izzy when
he plays video games.

177
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,677
They're absorbing the energy
from the beams of light,

178
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:51,113
like recharging the battery on a laptop.

179
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:53,170
Look!

180
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:03,620
Hey, look who we brought,
Digidestined from all over the world!

181
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:06,257
Who would have thought there'd be so many?

182
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:09,777
The gates opened up from all over the
world and they came to help us out.

183
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:13,337
And each one of them has a partner
Digimon who wants to help out too.

184
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:17,538
The bond between the Digidestined
and the Digimon opened up the gate.

185
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,490
Oh!

186
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,657
I knew it was true.

187
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:26,980
We were never really meant
to be the Digidestined.

188
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:28,640
We're not good enough.

189
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,468
What are you talking about?

190
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:33,915
Well, we don't have partner
Digimon like you guys have.

191
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:35,649
And all of us are tainted.

192
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:38,437
We still carry the dark
spores inside of us.

193
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:42,637
Because of them, the only thing we
have to look forward to is more pain.

194
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:43,550
Oh, no!

195
00:10:43,633 --> 00:10:45,089
The darkness is returning!

196
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:48,946
Yes, just keep thinking
that way, my children.

197
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:51,317
You guys, he's getting stronger!

198
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:54,377
It doesn't matter if you
don't have partner Digimon.

199
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:56,717
It doesn't matter if
you're not Digidestined.

200
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,637
You don't need any of that stuff
to have a really good life.

201
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,308
That's easy for you to say.

202
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,520
You have a Digimon.

203
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:06,137
We've all got shortcomings to face
and problems we wish we didn't have.

204
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:09,257
But you can't just lie down and
give in to all of your troubles.

205
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:10,170
Look at Ken.

206
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:12,997
He didn't give up when he
learned Oikawa was using him.

207
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:17,037
Everyone has problems, but everyone
has good things going for them, too.

208
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,017
Yeah, but what do we have?

209
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:22,020
What about all your hopes
and all of your dreams?

210
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:25,520
I think they're gone, or been taken away.

211
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:27,877
Geez, could you kids be
a little more negative?

212
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:31,437
The only person who can take your
dreams away is you by giving up on them.

213
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:32,880
So, what's your dream?

214
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:36,580
Well, I want to open a noodle cart. Huh?

215
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,200
Yeah, what's the matter with that?

216
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:42,477
I want to make the best noodles
in the whole wide world.

217
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,736
That's great, Davis.

218
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:50,300
Well, actually, I always wanted
to be a kindergarten teacher.

219
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:52,850
Me, too.

220
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:57,880
How about you?

221
00:11:58,160 --> 00:11:59,780
A baseball player.

222
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,727
I've always wanted a bakery.

223
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,842
I love the smell of fresh bread.

224
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:10,262
I wanted to draw comic books, but everyone
used to laugh at me, so I gave up on it.

225
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:12,397
I get it.

226
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:16,217
We all had dreams, but somehow
got the idea they were worthless.

227
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:19,359
So we gave up on them when
we shouldn't have, right?

228
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:22,617
Yeah, you can't let other people
talk you out of your dreams.

229
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:23,530
I wish.

230
00:12:23,613 --> 00:12:26,100
We hadn't wasted all
this time by giving up.

231
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:30,777
Don't worry, it's never too late to go
out and make your dreams become a reality.

232
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:34,742
Do you think that even kids like
us can make our dreams come true?

233
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:36,200
Of course, you bet.

234
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,720
Even me?

235
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:40,410
Absolutely.

236
00:12:40,493 --> 00:12:41,337
Absolutely for real?

237
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:43,480
Absolutely for real!

238
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:47,420
I feel so much happier.

239
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,740
I feel like I can do anything now.

240
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:52,800
You can if you believe. I do.

241
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:54,940
I believe in myself now.

242
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:00,480
Hey there, guys.

243
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,819
Well, aren't you glad to
meet your partner, Digimon?

244
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,080
Thanks for believing in us.

245
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:13,000
Oh, a digivice? For me?

246
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:14,520
It's hard to believe.

247
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:17,577
What's hard to believe is how smart
a handsome guy like me can be.

248
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:18,490
And humble.

249
00:13:18,573 --> 00:13:19,479
They're beautiful.

250
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:21,830
No!

251
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:23,540
This can't be happening!

252
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:26,540
These paltry children
can't make me disappear!

253
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,100
I won't allow it!

254
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,557
Quick, everybody, use your digivices,

255
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:33,522
and we'll get rid of this
pesky darkness forever!

256
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:48,600
Giga Crusher!

257
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,540
We did it!

258
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,620
We destroyed him!

259
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:15,330
Ah!

260
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:18,420
Hey, it's Gennai.

261
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:20,417
I have a present for you.

262
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,330
Here.

263
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:22,820
It's my tail ring.

264
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:25,517
Your tail ring was quite an
important little item, Gatomon.

265
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,477
It kept the dark powers of the Digimon

266
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:29,697
Emperor's fortress from
growing out of control.

267
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:32,133
And it allowed you all to DNA Digivolve.

268
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,117
And since that's not necessary
anymore, you get to have it back.

269
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,117
But do me a little favor.

270
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,240
No big deal,

271
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:38,997
but if you could keep it
away from the power-hungry

272
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,437
evil creatures looking to take
over and destroy the world,

273
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:42,461
that'd be great.

274
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:47,720
In all seriousness, you truly saved
the world. Thank you. To all of you.

275
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:51,357
We went to another world, too, different
than the real or digital worlds.

276
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,969
What was that weird place?

277
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:56,037
Believe it or not, it's a world
that can grant people's wishes.

278
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:58,944
Well, actually, it is the
power to grant wishes.

279
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:03,157
You know, the digital world also has some
of that power to make dreams come true.

280
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:08,880
So the digital world is basically a mix of
digital data and people's dreams. I see.

281
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,260
And that ocean.

282
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:14,126
Maybe it has the power to bring
people's dark thoughts to life.

283
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,808
What about the dark spores?

284
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:17,577
Shouldn't they all be taken out?

285
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:18,780
No, it's all right.

286
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:21,257
As long as we believe in
ourselves and our dreams,

287
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:24,057
the dark spores will remain
powerless against us.

288
00:15:24,140 --> 00:15:25,199
That's great, Ken.

289
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:27,770
Cody!

290
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,100
What are you doing?

291
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,177
Just a little further, Mr.

292
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:33,090
Oikawa.

293
00:15:33,173 --> 00:15:34,003
Don't give up now.

294
00:15:34,086 --> 00:15:35,980
I don't know if I can. Get up!

295
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,101
You have to try!

296
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:39,280
We're almost in the digital world!

297
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:41,420
Thank you, Cody.

298
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:47,117
If only I'd had your optimism, I might
not have ended up with such a sad fate.

299
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:50,237
But I was unable to maintain
hope through the bad times,

300
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,967
and I drowned in my despair.

301
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:56,440
If only I'd had friends like you,
or allowed myself to help me.

302
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:00,170
Yukio!

303
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:01,880
What's this?

304
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:03,840
Who is this Digimon?

305
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:05,780
I'm Datirimon.

306
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:07,880
I'm Yukio's partner Digimon.

307
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,620
Oikawa's partner Digimon?

308
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,560
Hey, check it out.

309
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:14,997
This little guy's here for you, Oikawa.

310
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:16,060
He's mine?

311
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:18,340
It's been a long time.

312
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:20,855
I've been waiting practically forever.

313
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:21,800
He's mine.

314
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,440
I don't believe it.

315
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:24,870
Wait a minute.

316
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,660
Don't you remember me?

317
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:28,680
Of course.

318
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,340
I remember you.

319
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,797
It's just been so long
since I've seen you.

320
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,060
Since my happier days with Hiroki.

321
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,797
Well, better late than never.

322
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,337
Come into the digital world.

323
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:40,596
This is your chance.

324
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:43,517
All you have to do is stand up
and walk into the digital world.

325
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,430
Come on.

326
00:16:44,513 --> 00:16:46,177
He may not have the strength, Cody.

327
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:50,084
His body was badly damaged by
having Malomyotismon inside of him.

328
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:53,860
I'm afraid he doesn't have
much time left. But no.

329
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,980
Is that the digital world?

330
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:01,920
It seems so rough somehow, unfinished.

331
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:04,837
A lot of energy was used
up to defeat Malomyotismon,

332
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:07,657
and as a result, the digital
world itself has been weakened.

333
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:09,857
I'm afraid it's going to take
a lot of hard work to get it

334
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:12,577
back to the way it used to be
before all of this happened.

335
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:14,540
The power of the other world.

336
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,320
The other world?

337
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:20,240
We can use it to make dreams come true.

338
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,157
So what do you plan to do?

339
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:25,360
My body is too weak to go
on, but I won't need it.

340
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:27,590
Wait!

341
00:17:27,673 --> 00:17:29,009
There must be another way!

342
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:35,774
Hold on to your optimism, your dreams,
and especially your friends, Cody.

343
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:39,617
Perhaps if I had been more like you,
I could have had adventures, too.

344
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:40,580
You still can!

345
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:45,117
You finally made it to the digital world
and found your partner Digimon, didn't you?

346
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,620
Mr. Owakawa!

347
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,940
Are you going so soon?

348
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,840
But we just met again!

349
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,330
Don't worry.

350
00:17:58,540 --> 00:18:01,187
I'll always be here
inside the digital world.

351
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:03,240
I shall protect it.

352
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,800
Goodbye, Digidestined.

353
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,700
And thank you!

354
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,557
Oikawa transformed himself
into energy and used

355
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:14,405
his life force to revitalize
the digital world.

356
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:19,541
He restored all of the beauty that was
almost completely destroyed by Malomiodasmon.

357
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:24,175
And Oikawa's spirit is still there
protecting the digital world forever.

358
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:26,970
Hey, Dad!

359
00:18:27,053 --> 00:18:29,040
Come on already, we have to go!

360
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:31,142
Right, we don't want to be late.

361
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:34,142
25 years have passed, and
I've become a novelist.

362
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:38,017
I'm working on a series of books about
our adventures in the digital world.

363
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:42,394
There have been a lot of big changes
in the world, and in us, since then.

364
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:44,217
Hey, everybody!

365
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:46,540
Look, it's TK! Hi! Hello!

366
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,980
TK, how are ya?

367
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:54,237
Now everyone on the planet knows about the
digital world and has their own partner,

368
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,150
Digimon.

369
00:18:55,233 --> 00:18:58,677
But despite all the changes that contact
with the digital world has brought,

370
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:01,277
one thing has remained
the same, our friendship.

371
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:03,217
We all still get together
and those gatherings

372
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,771
are some of the happiest times of my life.

373
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,917
Tai and Agumon are diplomats dealing with

374
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,317
relations between the
real and digital worlds.

375
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,180
And Tai finally cut his hair.

376
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,537
Hey, you wanna play tag? Yeah.

377
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:18,257
Matt and Gabumon became an astronaut
team and made it all the way to Mars,

378
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:21,357
even though they were only
supposed to go to the moon.

379
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,780
Now be careful, son.

380
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Oh, how come?

381
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:25,557
I'll take care of him.

382
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:27,457
Okay, and I'll take care of you.

383
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:29,577
Sora and Biyomon are fashion designers.

384
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:32,366
Biyomon says their new
line is just to die for.

385
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:33,640
Try to stay clean.

386
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:35,257
Nah, go roll in the mud.

387
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:36,997
Joe's the DigiWorld's first doctor.

388
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:39,297
Too bad his patients keep
eating his tongue depressors.

389
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:41,477
Now remember to share with the other kids.

390
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:42,390
Right!

391
00:19:42,473 --> 00:19:44,777
Mimi's cooking show is the only
time she takes off her hat.

392
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:46,537
Make sure you don't act like a ram cat.

393
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:47,450
Right.

394
00:19:47,533 --> 00:19:48,363
Or a sim chip.

395
00:19:48,446 --> 00:19:49,457
Izzy researches the digi world.

396
00:19:49,540 --> 00:19:51,257
He and his daughter
have their own language.

397
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:52,257
Ready to have fun?

398
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:53,170
Mm-hmm.

399
00:19:53,253 --> 00:19:54,083
Kari's a teacher.

400
00:19:54,166 --> 00:19:55,217
She actually likes being in school.

401
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:58,300
Now, whatever happens,
don't get all panicky, okay?

402
00:19:58,440 --> 00:20:00,558
But, Mom, that's what you always do.

403
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:04,397
Yoli and Ken are married with children,
and Ken and Stingmon are detectives.

404
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:07,657
But Yoli says he can't seem to detect
when it's his turn to do the dishes.

405
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:10,360
Hey, Dad, can I sue if I get tagged it?

406
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:11,737
Cody's a defense attorney.

407
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:14,997
He's bought a hundred briefcases
because Armadimon keeps sitting on them.

408
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:15,962
Hey, everybody.

409
00:20:16,220 --> 00:20:17,220
Sorry we're late.

410
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,880
Hey, Davis.

411
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:20,317
Glad you could finally make it.

412
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,377
Well, Davis finally
opened his noodle cart,

413
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:24,717
and believe it or not,
it became a huge success.

414
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:28,177
They're now Noodle Noodle, come get
your noodle carts all over the world.

415
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:30,577
What are you doing here
standing with your dad?

416
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:31,490
Go play tag.

417
00:20:31,573 --> 00:20:33,557
Yeah, go show what my tag's all about.

418
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:34,470
Oh, right.

419
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,300
So are you guys ready?

420
00:20:37,260 --> 00:20:38,090
Mm-hmm.

421
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,757
Come on, everybody.

422
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:40,817
Let's do it.

423
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,547
So you can see we're
still having adventures.

424
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:47,117
They're just a little different than the
ones we used to have when we were kids.

425
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,257
The darkness has not been conquered,

426
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:52,357
and it will continue to fight
against the light forever.

427
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:57,146
But as long as people remember to follow
their dreams, evil will be kept at bay.

428
00:20:57,520 --> 00:21:01,440
And on days like today, it's hard
to see any darkness anywhere.

429
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:05,977
Now it's up to our children and to
children everywhere to follow their dreams.

430
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,297
Who knows where they'll end up?

431
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:11,556
But the only way to find out is to
take that first step into adventure.

432
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:44,460
I'm going to run together with my
hands, and I'm going to run together

433
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:48,300
Why can't you give a big strength?
